    "callouts": [
      {
        "type": "the-purpose",
        "title": "Untitled",
        "body": "This topic set is designed to directly address your goal of advancing your skill in engineering 'Gemini Gems.' The topics provided below move beyond basic prompt engineering into the realm of true 'agentic' design. They cover the best practices you're asking about, such as building instruction sets that are not just lists of tasks, but comprehensive operational frameworks. The factors you might be missing, which these topics explore, include: 1) designing internal 'cognitive architectures' for the agent, 2) using structured syntax (like XML or pseudo-code) to enforce rules, 3) defining an agent's core 'constitution' or principles, and 4) building in explicit mechanisms for self-correction and context management. These inquiries are structured to provide a formal, deep-dive into crafting AI instruction sets that are robust, predictable, and capable of producing the high-quality, structured academic content you require for your PKB.",
        "line_number": 38,
        "source": "topic-set-advanced-strategies-in-agentic-instruction-set-engineering-for-academic-content-generation-🆔20251021030719.md",
