        },
        {
          "text": "**Simulated Tool Use:** Exploring how to instruct an LLM to \"simulate\" the use of tools it doesn't actually have access to (e.g., \"First, perform a simulated web search… now, based on those hypothetical results, write your analysis…\").",
          "indent_level": 1,
          "line_number": 114,
          "source": "topic-set-advanced-strategies-in-agentic-instruction-set-engineering-for-academic-content-generation-🆔20251021030719.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Dynamic Prompt Injection:** Investigating how an instruction set can tell the AI to *ask for* specific information from the user at certain points in the process, creating an interactive, multi-step workflow.",
          "indent_level": 1,
          "line_number": 119,
          "source": "topic-set-advanced-strategies-in-agentic-instruction-set-engineering-for-academic-content-generation-🆔20251021030719.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Error Handling & Graceful Degradation:** Writing instructions that define *how the agent should fail*—what to do when a request is ambiguous, contradictory to its principles, or beyond its capabilities (e.g., \"If the request is unclear, ask these three specific clarification questions…\").",
          "indent_level": 1,
          "line_number": 130,
          "source": "topic-set-advanced-strategies-in-agentic-instruction-set-engineering-for-academic-content-generation-🆔20251021030719.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Multi-Agent Simulation (Internal Monologue):** Crafting instruction sets that require the AI to \"think out loud\" by simulating a debate or discussion between multiple personas (e.g., \"As a 'Critic,' first argue against this point. Then, as a 'Proponent,' defend it.\") to achieve a more nuanced final answer.",
          "indent_level": 1,
          "line_number": 130,
          "source": "topic-set-advanced-strategies-in-agentic-instruction-set-engineering-for-academic-content-generation-🆔20251021030719.md"
        }
      ]
